---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button.astro';
import { ENGAGE_URL, CONTACT_URL } from '@/lib/site';

// Evidence page A (advisory package RB-07). Conservative by design: no program
// identifiers, no exact cluster size, no funding or percentage outcomes.
const constraints = [
  'Which artifacts can enter the environment at all?',
  'Which dependencies can be reproduced without external services?',
  'What is approved to run, and who approves it?',
  'How are versions, datasets, and results identified after the fact?',
  'What can an operator actually do when a workflow fails?',
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Secure ML Architecture"
  description="Operating ML inside restricted environments: controlled artifacts, reproducible dependencies, deployment boundaries, and the operator path that has to survive without connected conveniences."
>
  <section class="hero"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <span>EVIDENCE · SECURE &amp; CONSTRAINED ML</span>
    <h1>Secure ML architecture</h1>
    <p class="question">Buying question: can this ML system operate inside the environment we actually have?</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <p>A model pipeline is not deployable merely because it runs in a connected development environment. The deployment boundary determines which dependencies, data movements, artifacts, and operator actions can exist at all.</p>
    <p>My work has included distributed ML training and inference workflows in air-gapped, multi-GPU environments, spanning data preparation, orchestration, evaluation, deployment, and operator-facing workflows. The architectural problem is to make those parts function as one operating system for the work — not as a collection of demonstrations that depend on services unavailable at deployment.</p>

    <h2>The constraints come first</h2>
    <p>A useful review begins with the environment's actual constraints, because they settle the implementation before model selection or optimization can:</p>
    <ul class="constraints">{constraints.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}</ul>

    <h2>What transfers to a commercial team</h2>
    <p>For a team considering private or constrained AI deployment, the relevant lesson is not to copy a particular hardware stack. It is to make the system boundary explicit, identify the assumptions inherited from a connected environment, and test the operational path that has to survive without those conveniences.</p>

    <div class="boundary">
      <h3>Evidence boundary</h3>
      <p>This page describes publicly discussable experience at an architectural level. Program-specific configurations, handling details, and restricted artifacts are not reproduced here.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="dark"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Where this becomes an engagement</h2>
    <p>A focused architecture review can identify which operating assumptions have to change before a connected AI prototype can be delivered into a constrained environment.</p>
    <div class="ctas"><Button href={ENGAGE_URL} variant="brass">See engagement types →</Button><Button href={CONTACT_URL} variant="ghost">Discuss a review</Button></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .hero,.dark{background:var(--color-dark-surface);color:var(--color-dark-text);padding-block:var(--sp-20)}
  .hero span{font:var(--text-mono-meta);color:var(--color-brass);letter-spacing:.06em}
  .hero h1{font:var(--text-h1);margin-top:var(--sp-4)}
  .question{font:var(--text-body-lg);color:var(--color-dark-muted);margin-top:var(--sp-5);max-width:44em}
  .section{padding-block:var(--sp-16);border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-line)}
  .section p{font:var(--text-body);color:var(--color-slate);margin-top:var(--sp-5);max-width:42em}
  h2{font:var(--text-h2);margin-top:var(--sp-12)}
  .section h2:first-of-type{margin-top:var(--sp-12)}
  .constraints{margin:var(--sp-5) 0 0;padding-left:1.1em;max-width:42em;color:var(--color-slate);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--sp-3)}
  .boundary{margin-top:var(--sp-12);padding:var(--sp-6);border:1px solid var(--color-line);border-left:3px solid var(--color-brass);border-radius:var(--radius-card)}
  .boundary h3{font:var(--text-h3)}
  .boundary p{margin-top:var(--sp-3)}
  .dark h2{color:var(--color-dark-text);margin-top:0}
  .dark p{font:var(--text-body-lg);color:var(--color-dark-muted);margin-top:var(--sp-5);max-width:44em}
  .ctas{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:var(--sp-4);margin-top:var(--sp-8)}
  @media(max-width:768px){.hero,.dark{padding-block:var(--sp-14)}.section{padding-block:var(--sp-12)}}
</style>
